## Cisco Packet Tracer Network Lab

The Cisco Packet Tracer Network Lab was a hands-on networking project that I completed to strengthen my understanding of how devices communicate across a network.

Using Cisco Packet Tracer, I created different network topologies containing devices such as routers, switches, computers, and servers. I configured the devices and tested communication between different hosts to better understand how networks operate.

## What I Worked With

Throughout this project, I gained more experience with networking concepts such as:

- IP addressing
- Subnetting
- TCP/IP
- Routing
- Switching
- Cisco CLI commands
- Network troubleshooting
- Packet analysis

One of the most useful parts of this project was learning how to troubleshoot connectivity problems. Instead of only seeing whether something worked or did not work, I could follow packets through the simulated network and determine where communication was failing.

## What I Learned

This project helped me better understand how different networking concepts connect together. Configuring routers and switches gave me more practical experience compared to only learning about networking through notes or textbooks.

I also became more comfortable using Cisco-style command-line interfaces to configure devices and verify their configurations.

Overall, this project gave me a stronger networking foundation that I can apply to future work in information technology and cybersecurity.
